@description Rea-Sixty
@author Frank Acklin
@version 0.1.25
@changelog
  - Codename: Catch the Game Last Night?
  - New: Master track on the surfaces — show Master as Track 0 on UC1, UC1 Out-Gain drives the Master fader, Bus Compressor on the Master shows in the BC carousel, and pin the Master to UF8 Strip 1 / 8 (Replace strip or Shift banking)
  - New: Active CS / BC marker in REAPER's TCP/MCP Inserts list (opt-in, Settings → Device) — see at a glance which plug-in the surface is driving
  - New: Encoder Mode → FX Move (in chain) + fx_move action to shuffle the active FX up / down in the focused track's chain
  - New: Combine GR across plug-ins — optionally sum every compressor's gain reduction; separate UF8 / UC1 toggles
  - Polish: Device pane tidied, searchable combo-popup width fix, "Plug-in" spelt consistently throughout
